    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1605">

                <pb facs="1174" n="1058" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1058"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.51/105.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the French Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1449.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 4, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your excellency’s note of January 25, 1915, in which you ask the
                    Department to inform you [etc.]</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to inform your excellency that the Department appears
                    to have no information regarding the reported seizure of the rifles and
                    ammunition mentioned. However, a telegram has been sent to the American Consul
                    at Vera Cruz to report <pb facs="1175" n="1059" xml:id="pg1059"/> on the matter,
                    and when his report is received you will be promptly informed.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
